 "concept": "Red-brick Victorian factory: a wide machine hall with sawtooth north-light roof is the base mass, a tall clock tower attaches at its front corner as the ONE landmark (hip_steep roof, spire, clock on the south face). A furnace hall with chimneys and smokestacks sits behind it, a lower workshop wing and an office/storage block step down to the east. Red brick (minecraft:bricks) on pillar and wall2 so the facade reads red, stone brick base and copper trim as contrast, dark deepslate-tile roofs. Interiors are big: 11-12 high machine halls 15+ wide, tower floors wide enough to use. Details go outward: gears on the windowless furnace end wall, pipe rack on the process hall, smokestacks beside the furnace hall, a porch at the main entrance, a bridge across a yard gap to the workshop wing.",
